  "status": "PASS",
  "residual": "Genuine nonfinite regenerative profile K = epsilon*seed + (1-epsilon)*R, 0 < epsilon <= 1. The explicit geometric probability/invariance, bounded resolvent/Poisson solution, all-initial canonical bounded measurable averages and noncompact weak empirical convergence are proved. A predeclared numeric functional limit with default Phi(fallback) yields all four original typed path-law factorizations; compact descriptors additionally have a literal measurable probability-valued limit and fallback. The original full comparison sets/global dual-Lipschitz predicate and baseline contractions are retained in the generated original margin theorem; first moments of the constructed geometric laws explicitly discharge its finite-gap gate. A general global probability-valued weak-limit selector and unbounded-descriptor empirical-W1 tail/moment extension are separate scope."
